static const struct soc_device_attribute mt7621_pci_quirks_match[] = {
    { .soc_id = "mt7621", .revision = "E2" }
};
```
Reason:
The absence of a sentinel entry in the `mt7621_pci_quirks_match` array means that there is no proper termination of the quirks table. This causes the `soc_device_match_attr` function to continue reading beyond the intended end of the array, leading to an oops when it attempts to access invalid memory.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
+    { .soc_id = "mt7621", .revision = "E2" },
+    { /* sentinel */ }
};
```
Reason:
Adding a sentinel entry at the end of the `mt7621_pci_quirks_match` array properly terminates the quirks table. This allows the `soc_device_match_attr` function to correctly identify the end of the list, preventing it from accessing out-of-bounds memory and thus avoiding the kernel oops.

